  body: |
    # ESA basic and additional conditions in the source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source distinguishes basic conditions from additional ESA(Cont) or ESA(IR) conditions, the claim requirement and National Insurance number provisions.

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 41011–41013 must be read together with exceptions, mixed-age provisions and duration rules. LCW is one basic condition, not a sufficient entitlement decision. No current New Style ESA or UC test is inferred.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 41011, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=5)
    - [DMG 41012, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=6)
    - [DMG 41013, PDF page 6](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/689db34d1fedc616bb13399c/dmg-ch-41.pdf#page=6)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:28.939434Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

